        "depth": 1,
        "epoch": 1,
        "hypothesis": "Encoding each permutation into a reusable line buffer and writing it once should reduce per-character iostream overhead and per-line flushes. The affine indexed character stores have no data dependence between output positions, so the compiler may vectorize that formatting loop; lexicographic permutation traversal remains serial and unchanged.",
        "id": "d6755543c395449e",
        "ordinal": 1,
        "parent_id": null,
        "role": "B",
        "source_commits": [],
        "sources": [],
        "transformations": {
          "files": [
            "src/permutations.cc"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Replace per-character ostream insertion and std::endl flushing with a reusable output line and one std::cout.write call per permutation.",
            "Use affine indexed stores to place permutation characters into independent output positions; leave the dependency-sensitive permutation traversal unchanged."
          ]
        },
