        "hypothesis": "Partitioning the sorted permutation set by distinct first-byte prefixes lets OpenMP workers generate disjoint lexicographic ranges while the master emits them in order. A bounded handoff may overlap generation and output on the 4-core target, though output-bound cases may regress.",
        "id": "e75fe4cb72c8475b",
        "ordinal": 1,
        "parent_id": null,
        "role": "C",
        "source_commits": [],
        "sources": [],
